1
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,560
- TOKYO -

2
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:31,470
Tsubasa!

3
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:35,470
Be careful and don't wander off too far, okay?

4
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,080
Honestly...

5
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:42,560
Give him a football and he's perfectly happy.

6
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:43,720
Truly.

7
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,520
By the time this trip is over,
Tsubasa will be turning 2.

8
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:01,110
Don't let him forget you.

9
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,520
He won't cry this time.

10
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:08,000
Hey, where's Tsubasa?

11
00:01:08,230 --> 00:01:10,000
What? He was just here.

12
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:12,720
It's dangerous for him to wander off alone.

13
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:14,230
Tsubasa!

14
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,470
Tsubasa!

15
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:32,230
Tsubasa!

16
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:13,720
Episode 1
Soaring to the Sky
Translation: ARE-YOU-SURE
www.areyousuresubs.com

17
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:17,280
- 10 Years Later - Pacific Ocean -

18
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,720
Your son?

19
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:33,520
Yes, his name is Tsubasa.

20
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,680
But even though he's not on the football field...

21
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,160
...he posed in his uniform.

22
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,360
They're moving today.

23
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:45,840
He's letting you know he's moved to a new house.

24
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,320
Is that so.

25
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,950
And by the looks of it...

26
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:53,230
...this kid has no intention of helping
his mother at all.

27
00:03:54,230 --> 00:03:58,560
- Nankatsu - Shizuoka Region -

28
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:01,000
Take care of these.

29
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,160
Got it.

30
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:05,280
Tsubasa! Where have you disappeared to?

31
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:07,040
Come and give us a hand!

32
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:20,340
Mom, I'm going to go check out the city.

33
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:23,440
What?! Wait, Tsubasa!

34
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,400
Hey!

35
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:31,360
Oh, that boy...
He's done it again.

36
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:33,840
Your son really loves the ball.

37
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:35,160
Yes.

38
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:38,760
It's thanks to the ball that he's even alive.

39
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:41,680
That child...

40
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:44,600
...grew up alongside a football.

41
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,760
<i>It was truly like a miracle.</i>

42
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:51,600
<i>Tsubasa!</i>

43
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:04,840
<i>Tsubasa!</i>

44
00:05:06,110 --> 00:05:08,140
<i>When the car hit him...</i>

45
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:13,400
<i>...the football acted like a buffer
when he fell to the ground...</i>

46
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:16,800
<i>...so Tsubasa came out of it without a scratch.</i>

47
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,040
<i>Ever since that day, he's been all about football.</i>

48
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:25,520
Mount Fuji!

49
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:31,150
<i>As if he was born to play football.</i>

50
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:38,000
<i>So I've arrived in a new city!</i>

51
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,560
Hello!

52
00:06:03,950 --> 00:06:04,950
Excuse me!

53
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,840
Of course, go ahead.

54
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:27,430
# Nankatsu Elementary School #

55
00:06:28,110 --> 00:06:29,800
This is Nankatsu School.

56
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,400
Where is Shutetsu?

57
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,000
A football field!

58
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:58,000
Hey, Ishizaki, what is the meaning of this?

59
00:06:58,470 --> 00:07:00,600
Why did you bring elementary school students?

60
00:07:00,950 --> 00:07:01,840
What?!

61
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:04,430
According to our agreement...

62
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:07,430
...since we beat Nankatsu 10-0,
the field was supposed to stay with us.

63
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,430
Meaning, at Shutetsu.

64
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,560
Shut your mouth!

65
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:14,430
You already have your own field!

66
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,870
Leave this one to us!

67
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:19,680
Making a name for ourselves nationally
brought in new members.

68
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,950
That field is for our A team.

69
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:25,950
This one here is for the B team.

70
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,360
Did you say B team?!

71
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,720
Hey, Wakabayashi!

72
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:33,840
Just because you've achieved a bit in football
doesn't mean you can order us around!

73
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:37,230
This field is important for the lower grades!

74
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:39,280
Hand it over without a fight!

75
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,600
Captain...

76
00:07:41,110 --> 00:07:44,870
It's pretty obvious I'm not going to hand it over.

77
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,640
But you're not backing down either.

78
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:52,600
Then let's settle this with a competition.

79
00:07:52,950 --> 00:07:54,280
You'll compete with us?

80
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:56,760
Yes.

81
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,720
Each club captain...

82
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,680
...will take one shot.

83
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:05,040
Rugby, handball... It doesn't matter what it is.

84
00:08:05,950 --> 00:08:08,320
Come at me with your own sports.

85
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:17,360
From outside the penalty area...

86
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:19,760
...I bet I can stop every ball.

87
00:08:20,230 --> 00:08:21,800
If you want the field...

88
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,400
...come and try to score against me!

89
00:08:25,230 --> 00:08:26,640
What a guy...

90
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:32,680
If you manage to score even one goal,
the field is yours.

91
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,160
You little...

92
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:39,200
So you're serious.

93
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Alright!

94
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:45,810
Even if you are the young genius goalkeeper Wakabayashi...

95
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:50,200
...you have no chance of winning this contest!

96
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,760
The contest will show that.

97
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:00,430
I'll go first.

98
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:03,840
Watch and learn, Ishizaki.
I'll settle this in no time.

99
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,400
I'm counting on you, Senpai!

100
00:09:11,110 --> 00:09:12,560
Here it comes!

101
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:22,560
See? Unlike a football, you can't tell
where a rugby ball is going!

102
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,800
You did it, Captain!

103
00:09:34,430 --> 00:09:36,200
You're amazing, Captain!

104
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:38,640
That was one.

105
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:44,000
Okay, next is handball.

106
00:09:44,470 --> 00:09:48,000
A football is twice the size of a handball.

107
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:50,080
If I can't throw it in...

108
00:09:51,430 --> 00:09:54,110
...I'll be a disgrace to the handball team!

109
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:58,110
- No way!
- Unbelievable!

110
00:10:01,230 --> 00:10:03,920
Just what you'd expect from the genius goalkeeper Wakabayashi.

111
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,950
Don't praise him.

112
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:10,080
We can't give up our precious lower grades' field.

113
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,280
Now it's my turn.

114
00:10:13,430 --> 00:10:15,080
Senpai, I beg of you!

115
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:20,360
No matter how good you are, it's impossible to stop this.

116
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:23,870
If I can't throw this, I'll quit baseball.

117
00:10:26,230 --> 00:10:26,950
Come!

118
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,640
What's with that grin?!

119
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:32,950
Come!

120
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,640
Don't let him intimidate you!

121
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:37,280
Just throw it straight and as fast as you can!

122
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:38,230
Got it!

123
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,200
With this...

124
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,560
...this will be over!

125
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,840
How did he catch that?!

126
00:10:55,430 --> 00:10:57,430
This guy's a monster.

127
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,110
Who's next?

128
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:13,520
Amazing!

129
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:17,200
What happened? Is it over already?

130
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,360
Looks like it's over.

131
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,230
I'm the last one!

132
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:30,040
As a track athlete, what are you going to throw?

133
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
This.

134
00:11:33,230 --> 00:11:36,000
A javelin?! Isn't that too dangerous, Senpai?!

135
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:40,040
What? I covered the tip, so it's fine.

136
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,870
I don't care what it is.

137
00:11:43,110 --> 00:11:44,760
You arrogant snob.

138
00:11:48,110 --> 00:11:49,840
Let's see if you can stop this one!

139
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:51,720
Come.

140
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,040
He jumped!

141
00:12:12,110 --> 00:12:14,040
He kicked it!

142
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:20,520
Are you serious?

143
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,280
Then we're agreed.

144
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,560
Train properly.

145
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:29,200
Y-Yes, sir!

146
00:12:35,950 --> 00:12:39,640
I've never seen such an amazing goalkeeper before!

147
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,320
Senpai.

148
00:12:47,950 --> 00:12:49,720
Sorry, Ishizaki.

149
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,840
We should be training too.

150
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:55,200
Sorry, but give up on this field.

151
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:59,200
No way! This isn't how you solve a problem!

152
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:03,600
In this day and age, you can't even trust your senpai.

153
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:04,920
Ishizaki.

154
00:13:06,110 --> 00:13:07,430
Are you done?

155
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,920
We're going to train here.

156
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:12,870
Damn it!

157
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,800
What a show-off!

158
00:13:15,950 --> 00:13:17,920
Besides, we didn't even lose to you!

159
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:21,520
What?

160
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:25,920
Look, where did that goalkeeper from earlier go?

161
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:29,280
I don't know. He probably went home.

162
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,430
Can you tell me where his house is, then?

163
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:33,560
What are you going to do once you know?

164
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:35,680
I want to challenge him!

165
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,320
Challenge him?!

166
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:41,360
Are you stupid?!
Didn't you see him just now?!

167
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:44,160
- He even caught a baseball.
- Challenge!

168
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,920
But if you're that curious, I'll show you.

169
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:50,600
Thanks!

170
00:13:51,870 --> 00:13:54,080
What's your name?

171
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:56,680
I'm Ishizaki Ryo.

172
00:13:57,230 --> 00:13:59,600
And I'm Ozora Tsubasa.

173
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:07,950
Translation: ARE-YOU-SURE
www.areyousuresubs.com

174
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:19,600
By the way...

175
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:23,720
...you keep dribbling the ball, why is that?

176
00:14:23,950 --> 00:14:25,640
- I love it.
- The ball?!

177
00:14:27,110 --> 00:14:29,760
Football. Don't you love it too?

178
00:14:30,230 --> 00:14:32,360
Of course I do.

179
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:37,470
<i>He's actually quite talented.</i>

180
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:51,400
I see, you just moved here today, right?

181
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:54,320
From here you can see the whole city.

182
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:56,430
- Nice place, isn't it?
- Yes!

183
00:14:56,920 --> 00:14:58,000
Look, over there.

184
00:14:58,950 --> 00:15:01,430
Wakabayashi lives in that huge house.

185
00:15:02,470 --> 00:15:04,110
Over there? I see.

186
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:07,920
He's from one of the oldest families in the city.

187
00:15:10,950 --> 00:15:12,080
Hey, you--

188
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:24,720
How?

189
00:15:26,110 --> 00:15:29,160
Did you see Wakabayashi-kun's house too?

190
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,840
You want to challenge him as well?

191
00:15:33,230 --> 00:15:36,470
What are you doing?
Are you talking to the ball?

192
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,720
I'm glad we moved to this city.

193
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:41,920
I feel like interesting things are going to happen.

194
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:46,720
I'll live out my passion for football in this city.

195
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,760
L-Look, Ozora...

196
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:52,400
- You can just call me Tsubasa.
- Alright.

197
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:54,040
In that case, Tsubasa...

198
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:56,520
...I don't know what you're after, but...

199
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:59,950
...a newcomer like you can't beat Wakabayashi.

200
00:16:00,430 --> 00:16:03,320
He's someone who won the national tournament...

201
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:06,110
...and didn't concede a single goal.

202
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:07,680
And besides...

203
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:12,720
Hey! Are you even listening to what I'm saying?!

204
00:16:13,870 --> 00:16:15,560
What are you doing?!

205
00:16:17,870 --> 00:16:18,950
This will do.

206
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,230
What's this?

207
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:38,200
Hey, are you serious?

208
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:42,110
Do you really think you can send this ball
all the way to Wakabayashi's house?

209
00:16:44,230 --> 00:16:45,800
Here it comes!

210
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:55,520
There it is!

211
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:58,000
Go!

212
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,230
- This...
- ...is absurd!

213
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,230
What's wrong, Genzo?

214
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:20,400
That ball...

215
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:21,840
Mikami-san...

216
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:23,800
Where it came from...

217
00:17:24,430 --> 00:17:25,720
...is that hill over there.

218
00:17:25,950 --> 00:17:26,640
What?

219
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,600
You must be mistaken.

220
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:31,000
Do you know how far that is from here?

221
00:17:31,470 --> 00:17:32,320
But...

222
00:17:34,230 --> 00:17:35,920
<i># Ozora Tsubasa requests a match #</i>

223
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:38,320
Ozora Tsubasa...

224
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:42,840
A-Amazing! It went right to the spot!

225
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,720
I hope he accepts.

226
00:17:45,110 --> 00:17:47,080
You're incredible!

227
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:49,080
What an amazing kick!

228
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:51,040
How did you do it?

229
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:54,080
Do you have some kind of secret gadget?

230
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:56,080
Of course not.

231
00:17:56,430 --> 00:18:00,250
Still, you might actually have a chance
at beating Wakabayashi!

232
00:18:00,490 --> 00:18:01,450
He'll accept.

233
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:03,800
He'll definitely accept your challenge.

234
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:07,040
<i># Ozora Tsubasa requests a match #</i>

235
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:07,720
Genzo!

236
00:18:08,230 --> 00:18:11,720
You must have seen wrong.
It's impossible for it to come from there.

237
00:18:17,470 --> 00:18:19,520
Can someone stop that dog?!

238
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:20,780
Stop, John!

239
00:18:28,230 --> 00:18:29,160
Ugh...

240
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:30,200
Who are you?!

241
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:33,040
- It's the paparazzi, I'm calling the police.
- Wait, hold on!

242
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:34,640
I'm not paparazzi.

243
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:38,720
I was just following the ball
that came from the hill...

244
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:42,000
...and ended up here.

245
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:45,560
So this ball really did come from--

246
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:49,560
Also, the one who kicked it is a kid,
just like me.

247
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:50,720
You said a kid?!

248
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:53,840
This isn't an adult's handwriting.

249
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:00,520
- Here.
- Thanks.

250
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:03,870
You have to beat Wakabayashi for sure.

251
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:05,520
For the sake of this ice cream!

252
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:12,920
Before the challenge, you should say...

253
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:20,520
...that if you beat him, he has to give
that football field to us at Nankatsu.

254
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:21,950
Why?

255
00:19:22,280 --> 00:19:23,280
Why?

256
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:28,160
Didn't you see that contest between Wakabayashi
and the upperclassmen just now?

257
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:29,320
I saw it, but...

258
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,950
...since there are already two goals...

259
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:35,520
...each team can use them instead of fighting.

260
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:39,600
<i>Ozora Tsubasa...</i>

261
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:41,470
<i>Who is he?</i>

262
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,400
<i>He kicked the ball from that hill.</i>

263
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:49,040
<i>If he's challenging me, is he from Nankatsu?</i>

264
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:50,470
<i>No.</i>

265
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:54,760
<i>There's no one in that football club
who can kick that well.</i>

266
00:19:57,870 --> 00:19:58,840
<i>Wait a second.</i>

267
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:03,230
<i>But no elementary school student
could kick it that hard either.</i>

268
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:04,840
<i>Yes.</i>

269
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,760
<i>Even with that bad handwriting, he must be
a middle school or high school student.</i>

270
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:10,600
Mikami-san.

271
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:13,840
Is something wrong, Mikami-san?

272
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:14,920
Yes.

273
00:20:15,470 --> 00:20:18,110
I feel like I've seen that man somewhere before.

274
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:20,280
That drunk?

275
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:24,430
Look.

276
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:26,840
This is that football field from earlier.

277
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:27,800
Yes.

278
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:29,840
Exactly.

279
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,200
A child can't kick that far.

280
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:36,520
Even for you, Genzo, it's a bit impossible.

281
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:37,760
Yes.

282
00:20:40,950 --> 00:20:42,230
It's Wakabayashi!

283
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,080
Look.

284
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:44,470
He's holding the ball.

285
00:20:44,950 --> 00:20:46,720
He's taken my challenge.

286
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:52,760
Wakabayashi, glad you came!

287
00:20:53,110 --> 00:20:56,320
This is the one who challenged you!

288
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:59,840
- What did you say?
- Such a small child...

289
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:05,720
Don't be ridiculous!

290
00:21:05,870 --> 00:21:09,160
A newcomer like him can't kick that powerfully!

291
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:11,400
He can, he can!

292
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:13,950
I saw it with my own eyes!

293
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,280
Very well...

294
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:19,000
Whether it's true or not...

295
00:21:19,230 --> 00:21:21,200
...we'll see the answer right now!

296
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:23,760
Here!

297
00:21:25,360 --> 00:21:26,870
Watch out! Here it comes!

298
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:35,110
<i>He changed the direction of the ball I kicked!</i>

299
00:21:40,230 --> 00:21:41,180
You...

300
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,600
Stop! The bus is coming!

301
00:21:59,430 --> 00:22:00,470
Wakabayashi-kun.

302
00:22:00,870 --> 00:22:03,110
Accept my challenge.

303
00:22:06,520 --> 00:22:07,280
You...

304
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:09,470
...are Ozora Tsubasa.

305
00:22:10,230 --> 00:22:13,720
Yes, I am Ozora Tsubasa!

307
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:59,920
Next Episode: Flying!